{"repositoryId":1212704894,"availability":"available","full":"sb2bg/marionette","name":"marionette","description":"Marionette is a deterministic simulation testing (DST) library for Zig.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Zig","stars":93,"forks":2,"created":"2026-04-16T16:41:13Z","updated":"2026-10-04T19:29:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sb2bg.github.io/marionette/","topics":["deterministic-simulation-testing","distributed-systems","simulation-testing","std-io","storage-testing","zig"],"demo":"https://sb2bg.github.io/marionette/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:07.937Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:07.937Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:07.937Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T05:07:07.937Z","stars":93,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Deterministic I/O and simulation testing for Zig.","Marionette makes failures involving time, disk, networking, and cooperative concurrency reproducible. Write production-shaped code against std.Io, run it under deterministic simulation, inject faults from your test, and replay a failure from its recorded decisions, configuration, and trace.","The long-term target is a deterministic std.Io for Zig. Today, Marionette provides the simulator, fault models, structured traces, replay checks, and the current file, network, and scheduler-backed I/O subsets needed to test real systems code."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sb2bg/marionette/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b565434ccf9140778308a51f4e173a3974d2b2b1688109a5d74c9f917b6fdf2c","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:08.017Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:08.017Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Deterministic I/O and simulation testing for Zig.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sb2bg/marionette/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"b565434ccf9140778308a51f4e173a3974d2b2b1688109a5d74c9f917b